{{~##
   One declared record type, and the levels inside it that are its own.

   **A struct is an entity beside a table and an enum, so it gets a file like one.** The
   declaration says "this is one type", and the generated code says the same thing only if
   there is one type - so this is written once however many groups named it. Declaring it
   inside each of those tables would give them a `Reward` apiece that share a name and are not
   the same type, and then nothing can be written that takes one.
   spec/types/declared-struct-identity.md.

   The body is the same include a table uses for a group nobody declared, so the two cannot
   drift. It is written for the nested case, which is four spaces deeper than a type at
   namespace level - so it is captured and dedented by one level rather than kept twice.
##~}}
{{ include 'csharp-file-head.sbn' ~}}
{{~ for rt in record.types ~}}
{{~ if !for.first }}

{{ end ~}}
{{~ if rt.is_outermost ~}}
{{~ for line in record.comment ~}}
{{~ if for.first ~}}
    /// <summary>
{{~ end ~}}
    /// {{ line }}
{{~ if for.last ~}}
    /// </summary>
{{~ end ~}}
{{~ end ~}}
{{~ if record.comment | array.size == 0 ~}}
    /// <summary>One <c>{{ record.name }}</c>, as the declaration that names it says.</summary>
{{~ end ~}}
{{~ else ~}}
    /// <summary>A record inside <see cref="{{ record.name }}"/>.</summary>
{{~ end ~}}
{{~ capture body ~}}
{{ include 'csharp-record-body.sbn' ~}}
{{~ end ~}}
{{~## One replace, not two: the eight-space pattern matches the front of every deeper line as
      well, so each loses exactly one level. A newline goes in front so the first line is
      reached the same way as the rest, and comes off again after. ##~}}
{{ ("\n" + body) | string.replace("\n        ", "\n    ") | string.slice 1 | string.rstrip }}
{{~ end ~}}
{{ include 'csharp-file-foot.sbn' ~}}
